From 11957c9bac1878d9ca274adba4ea80e15ea21be4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:55:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 60/60] Silent kits and audio tracks: check the silence before
 setting up the effects

A kit or audio track whose clip renders nothing and whose effects have given out
exact silence for 4096 samples skips its effects (v12). But renderOutput() only
found that out after setting all of them up for every block: the volume, pitch
and reverb conversions, FilterSet::setConfig(), the delay's working state, and a
cleared buffer for the render - about 550 instructions and 25 SDRAM lines per
track and call, 24.7k instructions per call for the 45 of a big project, where
nothing sounds.

GlobalEffectableForClip::renderOutput() now checks the same condition first,
from what it is made of before the setup:
- no sound came in last time and the effects have been silent long enough (as
  before);
- no clipping, compressor, recording, stutter, sample rate reduction or mod FX
  (the same reads as the check);
- the delay has no buffers and no repeats to wait for: then
  createDelayWorkingState() with no sound coming in allocates none (doDelay
  false) and only notes that no sound is coming in, which Delay::process()
  sets again before it reads it; an old file's delay time change goes the old
  way;
- the filters' modes stay as FilterSet::setConfig() last left them
  (FilterSet::keepsModes()): a mode change resets a filter, so it goes the old
  way; otherwise setConfig() only sets what processFilters() reads after
  setting it again;
- hasNothingToRender(): a kit with no drum rendering and no drone row sounding,
  an audio track neither playing its clip's sample nor echoing an input, i.e.
  renderGlobalEffectableForClip() would render nothing and return false.
Then renderWithNothingToRender() does exactly what the old path did besides the
setup: the sidechain (hits and envelope), the compressor's threshold and reset,
the kit rows' automation (Kit::tickNoteRowParamManagers(), split out of
renderGlobalEffectableForClip()), the reverb kept awake while the track sends
to it, postReverbVolumeLastTime and the clip's automation. Anything else takes
the old path unchanged, so the output is the same, bit for bit.

Kit::renderNonAudioArpPostOutput() walked all rows of the active clip every
block for MIDI, gate and drone rows' own arpeggiators; a kit of sound rows only
(numNonAudioDrums, counted as numDroneDrums) now returns at once. The kit arp's
settings are still refreshed every block: its note probability and spreads
apply with the arp off too (Arpeggiator::noteOn(), calculateRandomizerAmounts()).

